body:
I did a quick test in `main()`.

```rust
use std::env;
println!("current_exe: {:?} {:?}", std::env::current_exe(), std::env::current_exe().map(|v| std::fs::canonicalize(v)));

for argument in env::args() {
    println!("ARG> {} {:?}", argument.clone(), std::fs::canonicalize(argument));
}
```

I created an hardl link (test_hardlink) pointing to starship and I got:
```
current_exe: Ok("/home/bbigras/test_hardlink") Ok(Ok("/home/bbigras/test_hardlink"))
ARG> ./test_hardlink Ok("/home/bbigras/test_hardlink")
thread 'main' panicked at 'not yet implemented', src/main.rs:28:5
note: run with `RUST_BACKTRACE=1` environment variable to display a backtrace.
```

